  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "There are only two triangles with integer side lengths of perimeter $10$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What are the side lengths of these two triangles?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3,3,4)$ and $(2,4,4)$.",
          "worked": "Write the sides in increasing order as $a\\le b\\le c$. The triangle inequality gives $c<10-c$, so $c<5$. Also, $10=a+b+c\\le3c$, so the integer $c$ is $4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a+b&=10-4\\\\a+b&=6\\end{align*}$$\nWith $a\\le b\\le4$, the only pairs are $(2,4)$ and $(3,3)$. Hence the triangles have sides $(2,4,4)$ and $(3,3,4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Which of these two triangles has the larger area?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p14-q4-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The triangle with sides ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(3,3,4)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " has the larger area.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p14-q4-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heron’s formula gives areas ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sqrt{20}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sqrt{15}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " square units, respectively.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Both triangles have semi-perimeter $s=\\frac{10}{2}=5$.\nFor sides $(3,3,4)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A_1&=\\sqrt{5(5-3)(5-3)(5-4)}\\\\A_1&=\\sqrt{20}\\end{align*}$$\nFor sides $(2,4,4)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A_2&=\\sqrt{5(5-2)(5-4)(5-4)}\\\\A_2&=\\sqrt{15}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\sqrt{20}>\\sqrt{15}$, the triangle with sides $(3,3,4)$ has the larger area.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
